PDFTools (also known as pdf-tools, PdfTools or pdftools) is a
collection of minor-modes centered around a server querying [[PDF]]
documents for all kinds of information.

It supports:
* [https://www.emacswiki.org/emacs/IncrementalSearch|Isearch]ing documents,
* browsing PDF Outlines via [https://www.emacswiki.org/emacs/ImenuMode|Imenu],
* following internal and external links,
* copying text with the mouse and
* some other stuff.

It was originally developed by [https://github.com/politza politza] on
[https://github.com/politza/pdf-tools GitHub].  There were screenshots
at politza's university
homepage.[http://www.hochschule-trier.de/~politza/emacs/pdf-tools.png]
However he archived that repository in 2022.

Now pdf-tools is developed at [https://github.com/vedang/pdf-tools
Vedang Manerikar’s GitHub repo].  There's a homepage at:
https://pdftools.wiki/

pdf-tools is available in [[MELPA]] and [https://elpa.nongnu.org/nongnu/ Non-GNU ELPA].

